From ed986c67ed467a3477679eaadcc28aa23813757a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:45:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Optional authentication (AUTH_REQUIRED) with a sign-in
 screen

Login endpoints existed but no endpoint required a session, e.g.
DELETE /api/security-events/{id} worked anonymously.

Backend
- AUTH_REQUIRED=true makes every HTTP endpoint except /health, /api/auth/*
  and the API docs return 401 without a valid session cookie; the WebSocket
  is closed with code 1008. Default stays off so the demo/Lovable preview is
  unaffected.
- The auth middleware sits inside CORS, so 401 responses carry CORS headers
  and the browser can react to them.
- With AUTH_REQUIRED=true the backend refuses to start while SESSION_SECRET
  is still the default value.
- GET /api/auth/config -> {"auth_required": bool}.

Frontend
- On startup the console asks /api/auth/config; if a login is required and
  there is no session it shows a sign-in screen (also after any 401).
- After sign-in the operator name/role come from the session user, the
  WebSocket is opened and data refreshed; a sign-out button is shown.
- Operator initials are derived from the name instead of hard-coded "RV".

README documents the environment variables. Tests: tests/test_auth_required.py.

