 2. At this project root: `npm install; npm run dev`
 3. Open the V2 console. It connects to `http://localhost:8000`; set `VITE_API_URL` for another backend address.
 
+### Authentication (optional)
+
+By default the API is open so the demo console works without a login. To require a session for every API call and the WebSocket, start the backend with:
+
+```
+AUTH_REQUIRED=true SESSION_SECRET=<long random value> python -m uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000
+```
+
+The console then shows a sign-in screen (demo user from `DEMO_USER_EMAIL` / `DEMO_USER_PASSWORD`, default `operator@seashield.local` / `seashield-demo`). The backend refuses to start with `AUTH_REQUIRED=true` and the default secret.
+
+The local database (`backend/seashield.db`) is not tracked in git; it is created on first start.
+
 V2 hydrates vessels, cameras, events, incidents, simulation actions, and WebSocket updates from V1.8. V2-only device telemetry remains explicitly simulated until V1.8 supplies equivalent API endpoints.
 
